NOTE ON SCOPE

This licence covers the code and analysis scripts in this repository only.

It does NOT cover:

  - The challenge dataset (proband WGS and clinical summary), which is
    controlled-access and remains subject to the Sage Bionetworks data use
    terms. Raw genomic files and the complete source clinical record are excluded;
    bounded case-derived findings and selectors are included.

  - The written reports, figures and team-authored documentation, which are
    licensed CC BY 4.0: https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/.

  - Third-party reference resources referenced by the workflow (GRCh38,
    ClinVar, gnomAD, VEP, REVEL, AlphaMissense, Exomiser, HPO), each of which
    carries its own licence and must be obtained from its original source.

  - Database-derived drug-census tables in workflow/track2-drug-census/.
    ChEMBL-derived data retain CC BY-SA 3.0 terms; DrugCentral-derived data
    retain CC BY-SA 4.0 terms; UniProt data retain CC BY 4.0 terms.
    Broad Repurposing Hub metadata retain the source-specific notices
    recorded in workflow/track2-drug-census/broad-hub-review.md and its
    linked summary. Their
    source-qualified provenance and attribution are documented in that
    directory's README. Neither the MIT code option nor the team-authored
    submission grant overrides those third-party terms.

HACKATHON SUBMISSION GRANT

The MVA Hackathon terms require submitted participant code, reports and other
team-authored outputs to be available under CC BY 4.0. For the team's own material
included in a submission, that grant applies in addition to the MIT option for
code above. It does not relicense third-party dependencies or grant access to the
controlled dataset. Keeping this working repository private does not waive the
submission terms or satisfy the later public-release requirement.

Official terms:
